Data license and attribution

The growth-curve records converted into data/bw25113_round01 through
data/bw25113_round07, and the derived tables under results/, originate from:

Honoka Aida and Bei-Wen Ying. Population Dynamics of Escherichia coli Growing
under Chemically Defined Media. Scientific Data 12, 984 (2025).
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-05356-3

The source workbooks are deposited on Figshare and declared under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International license (CC BY 4.0):

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

A frozen snapshot of the nine source workbooks, with per-file checksums, is
maintained in the companion repository:

https://github.com/pinheiroGroup/chemical-media-dataset

You may share and adapt the material for any purpose provided that appropriate
credit is given, a link to the license is supplied, and changes are indicated.
Derived tabular and JSON data in this repository were produced from those
source files and should retain the same source attribution.

